-- title:
--   Claim 7 — Bounded annihilator and APS criterion
-- statement:
--   Let $n\ge1$, let $k$ be a field and let $f=(f_1,\ldots,f_{n+1})$ be a minimally dependent tuple in $k[X_1,\ldots,X_n]$. Put $\Delta=\max_i\deg f_i$ and $K=\overline k$. There is an irreducible $H\in k[Y_1,\ldots,Y_{n+1}]$ such that
--   $$\ker(k[Y]\to k[X])=(H),\qquad\ker(K[Y]\to K[X])=(H),\qquad\deg H\le\Delta^{n+1},$$
--   where both maps are the canonical substitutions $Y_i\mapsto f_i$, and
--   $$\mathrm{APS}(f)\iff H(0)=0.$$
--   The kernel equalities encode the canonical quotient presentations of the coordinate subalgebras. Minimal dependence in positive dimension implies that each coordinate is nonconstant.
--
--   This is the full presentation, degree and APS criterion, extending the existing Open principal-generator subclaim rather than posing that subclaim separately.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: The coefficient field is rational or finite. → The algebraic statement is quantified over every field, with the stated algebraic closures and valuation where used.; reason: The algebraic arguments use no restriction on the base field; specializing to a rational or finite field gives the entire source statement.
--   - encoding: Canonical coordinate-algebra quotient presentations before and after extending scalars, for the nonconstant minimally dependent regime. → Equalities of canonical evaluation kernels with the ideal generated by H, with n at least one.; reason: The first isomorphism theorem makes these the same presentations; in positive dimension minimal dependence already implies nonconstant coordinates.
-- source:
--   Nikhil Balaji, Mahsa Shirmohammadi, Sébastien Tavenas, James Worrell, STOC 2027 submission #1125 (October 2026), Claim 7, p.18 (PDF p.18); https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/1125.pdf#page=18

import Definitions.Def_ApproxPolySatCH_Main_ResultantLanguages

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace ApproxPolySatCH.Main

theorem annihilator_presentation {k : Type} [Field k] {n : ℕ}
    (hn : 1 ≤ n) (f : Fin (n + 1) → Poly k n)
    (hf : MinimallyDependent f) :
    ∃ H : Poly k (n + 1), AnnihilatorPresentation f H ∧
      H.totalDegree ≤ maxDegree f ^ (n + 1) ∧
      (APS f ↔ MvPolynomial.eval (0 : Fin (n + 1) → k) H = 0) := by sorry

end ApproxPolySatCH.Main
